<v Elia Einhorn>She's asleep. She's asleep. I am going to-- I just saw Amy. I get to see her like three times a day for two minutes. And I said to her, we are going to have to do such a strict regimen to get this kid back to normal life after this because I am like-- you know, I'm trying to keep her life as normal as possible.
<v Elia Einhorn>她睡着了，她睡着了。我打算——我刚看到艾米。我每天大概能见她三次，每次两分钟。我对她说，我们必须制定非常严格的制度，在这之后让孩子恢复正常生活，因为我——你知道，我尽量让她的生活尽可能正常。

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:21.020
<v Elia Einhorn>So because she already can't see Amy, she can't go outside-- so I am just like-- I've become the biggest fucking pushover. I said to Amy, she had like a tasting menu before bed.
<v Elia Einhorn>所以因为她已经见不到艾米，也出不去——所以我简直变成了最大的软蛋。我对艾米说，她睡觉前简直像在享受一份品鉴菜单。

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:34.520
<v Elia Einhorn>We usually let her have a little snack if she wants it. She's adding things, having me get up and go to the kitchen and get more stuff. And I, like, can hardly handle getting up to go get her something. It's just like, oh, dude.
<v Elia Einhorn>我们通常让她吃点小零食，如果她想吃的话。她一直在加东西，让我起床去厨房拿更多。而我，几乎无法支撑自己起床去给她拿东西。简直是，噢，老兄。

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:40.150
<v Elia Einhorn>So she must have had bites of like seven snacks. And it's ridiculous. But I just wanted her to--
