00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:48.060
<v Elia Einhorn>But with all this research about the viral load buildup, we've had an infectious disease doctor that we've been talking to that said, you know, don't do that. You can snuggle her if you need to because she's a toddler. You can't control that. But like, as little as possible, so I try to put her between my legs or have my foot on her just to touch her a little bit, you know.
<v Elia Einhorn>但考虑到关于病毒载量积累的所有研究，我们一直在咨询的一位传染病医生说，你知道，别那么做。如果需要，你可以拥抱她，因为她是个蹒跚学步的孩子。你控制不了那个。但要尽可能少，所以我试着把她放在我双腿之间或者把我的脚放在她身上，只是为了稍微触碰她一下，你知道。

