00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:41.190
<v Elia   Einhorn>On the one hand, she's doing fine. And on the other hand, she's really feeling her age equivalent of like really lonely and cut off. She keeps talking to me about how sick Amy is. And I tell her like, you know, mom is sick. But mom's getting better.
<v Elia   Einhorn>一方面，她表现得很好。另一方面，她真的感到了与她年龄相当的孤独和被隔绝。她一直跟我谈论艾米病得有多重。我告诉她，你知道，妈妈生病了。但妈妈正在好转。

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:51.020
<v Elia   Einhorn>And I didn't even tell her I was sick, but she somehow figured it out. And I don't know if it's the mask, or what. So she says, daddy's sick. And I said, daddy's a little bit sick, but he's OK.
<v Elia   Einhorn>我甚至没告诉她我生病了，但她不知怎么就发现了。我不知道是因为口罩，还是其他什么原因。所以她说，爸爸生病了。我说，爸爸有点生病，但他没事。

00:20:51.020 --> 00:21:10.320
<v Elia   Einhorn>I mean, I feel traumatic, feeling so upset about it. But again, it's like-- like, are these the last conversations that I'm ever going to have with her?
<v Elia   Einhorn>我的意思是，我觉得很痛苦，因为这感到非常难过。但再说一次，就像——这些是我和她最后谈话的机会吗？

